  <sysml:Requirement xmi:id='nist_cand_RS-2_c0_st' base_Class='nist_cand_RS-2_c0' Id="AU-6" Text="[CANDIDATE, medium confidence] Implement AU-6 for RS-2. Proposed from D3FEND Network Traffic Analysis, Client-server Payload Profiling, Network Traffic Community Deviation, Inbound Session Volume Analysis, Credential Compromise Scope Analysis, User Behavior Analysis (table entry 'Network Traffic Analysis', technique); relevant attack-tree leaves: Device on 1553 bus successfully sends adversary spoofed message to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Adversary steals key from SIPR connected ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Other NAV sensor spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; Adversary breaks encryption to determine the command link key to fly UAS to adversary selected location; MIL GPS spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; Adversary gets insider to give them the command link key to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected DoS cyber attack to degrade UAS operations; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to gain mission planning and AV location data; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack to employ ordnance on a target of their choice; Adversary maliciously modifies flight-critical software during development to alter AV mission computer. Rationale: technique entry 'Network Traffic Analysis' in nist80053_d3fend.json: Inbound/outbound traffic monitoring, anomaly analysis, audit review. (D3FEND countermeasure was medium-confidence)"/>
  <sysml:Requirement xmi:id='nist_cand_RS-2_c1_st' base_Class='nist_cand_RS-2_c1' Id="SI-4(11)" Text="[CANDIDATE, medium confidence] Implement SI-4(11) for RS-2. Proposed from D3FEND Network Traffic Analysis, Client-server Payload Profiling, Network Traffic Community Deviation, Inbound Session Volume Analysis (table entry 'Network Traffic Analysis', technique); relevant attack-tree leaves: Device on 1553 bus successfully sends adversary spoofed message to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Other NAV sensor spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; Adversary breaks encryption to determine the command link key to fly UAS to adversary selected location; MIL GPS spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected DoS cyber attack to degrade UAS operations; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to gain mission planning and AV location data; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack to employ ordnance on a target of their choice; Adversary maliciously modifies flight-critical software during development to alter AV mission computer. Rationale: technique entry 'Network Traffic Analysis' in nist80053_d3fend.json: Inbound/outbound traffic monitoring, anomaly analysis, audit review. (D3FEND countermeasure was medium-confidence)"/>
  <sysml:Requirement xmi:id='nist_cand_RS-2_c2_st' base_Class='nist_cand_RS-2_c2' Id="SI-4(4)" Text="[CANDIDATE, medium confidence] Implement SI-4(4) for RS-2. Proposed from D3FEND Network Traffic Analysis, Network Traffic Signature Analysis, Client-server Payload Profiling, Network Traffic Community Deviation, Inbound Session Volume Analysis (table entry 'Network Traffic Analysis', technique); relevant attack-tree leaves: Device on 1553 bus successfully sends adversary spoofed message to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Other NAV sensor spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; Adversary breaks encryption to determine the command link key to fly UAS to adversary selected location; MIL GPS spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected DoS cyber attack to degrade UAS operations; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to gain mission planning and AV location data; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack to employ ordnance on a target of their choice; Adversary maliciously modifies flight-critical software during development to alter AV mission computer. Rationale: technique entry 'Network Traffic Analysis' in nist80053_d3fend.json: Inbound/outbound traffic monitoring, anomaly analysis, audit review. (D3FEND countermeasure was medium-confidence)"/>
  <sysml:Requirement xmi:id='nist_cand_RS-2_c3_st' base_Class='nist_cand_RS-2_c3' Id="AC-4" Text="[CANDIDATE, medium confidence] Implement AC-4 for RS-2. Proposed from D3FEND Network Traffic Filtering, Inbound Traffic Filtering (table entry 'Network Traffic Filtering', technique); relevant attack-tree leaves: Device on 1553 bus successfully sends adversary spoofed message to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Other NAV sensor spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; MIL GPS spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected DoS cyber attack to degrade UAS operations; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to gain mission planning and AV location data; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack to employ ordnance on a target of their choice; Adversary maliciously modifies flight-critical software during development to alter AV mission computer. Rationale: technique entry 'Network Traffic Filtering' in nist80053_d3fend.json: Deny-by-default / allow-by-exception and information flow enforcement. (D3FEND countermeasure was medium-confidence)"/>
