  <sysml:Requirement xmi:id='nist_cand_RS-2_c8_st' base_Class='nist_cand_RS-2_c8' Id="SI-4" Text="[CANDIDATE, medium confidence] Implement SI-4 for RS-2. Proposed from D3FEND Network Traffic Signature Analysis, Database Query String Analysis (table entry 'Network Traffic Signature Analysis', technique); relevant attack-tree leaves: Device on 1553 bus successfully sends adversary spoofed message to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Other NAV sensor spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; MIL GPS spoofing to fly AV to adversary selected location; SIPR connected DoS cyber attack to degrade UAS operations; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack on ground station to gain mission planning and AV location data; SIPR connected Traditional-IT cyber attack to employ ordnance on a target of their choice; Adversary maliciously modifies flight-critical software during development to alter AV mission computer. Rationale: technique entry 'Network Traffic Signature Analysis' in nist80053_d3fend.json: Signature-based intrusion / malicious code detection. (D3FEND countermeasure was medium-confidence)"/>
  <sysml:Requirement xmi:id='nist_cand_RS-2_c9_st' base_Class='nist_cand_RS-2_c9' Id="IA-2" Text="[CANDIDATE, medium confidence] Implement IA-2 for RS-2. Proposed from D3FEND Agent Authentication, Biometric Authentication (table entry 'Agent Authentication', technique); relevant attack-tree leaves: Adversary steals key from SIPR connected ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Adversary breaks encryption to determine the command link key to fly UAS to adversary selected location; Operator insider gains access to ground station to fly AV to adversary selected location; Adversary supply chain attack on logistics system provides logical access to fly UAS to adversary selected location; Adversary gets insider to give them the command link key to fly AV to adversary selected location. Rationale: technique entry 'Agent Authentication' in nist80053_d3fend.json: Identification and authentication of users, devices and non-organizational users. (D3FEND countermeasure was medium-confidence)"/>
